Using the VS Code MCP RAG Extension
This VS Code extension creates a seamless integration between your MCP RAG server and the Coder agent. Here's how to use it:
Setup and Installation

Create a new VS Code extension project:
bashCopynpm init vscode-extension vscode-mcp-rag
cd vscode-mcp-rag

Copy the provided files into the project:

package.json (extension manifest)
src/extension.ts (main extension code)
resources/mcp-icon.svg (extension icon)


Install dependencies:
bashCopynpm install axios
npm install --save-dev @types/node @types/vscode

Build the extension:
bashCopynpm run compile

Install the extension by pressing F5 in VS Code or packaging it as a VSIX file:
bashCopynpm run vscode:prepublish
npx vsce package


Features
The extension provides these key features:

Code Context Search: Search your codebase for relevant snippets based on your query.
Project Reindexing: Trigger reindexing of your project directory.
Coder Agent Integration: Send searched context and queries to your Coder agent.
Context Exploration: View and navigate through found code snippets.
Query History: Keep track of your past queries for easy reuse.

Commands

MCP: Connect to RAG Server: Connect to your running MCP RAG server
MCP: Search Code Context: Search for relevant code in your project
MCP: Reindex Project: Reindex your project directory
MCP: Send to Coder Agent: Send selected context to the Coder agent

Integration with Coder Agent
The extension assumes your Coder agent accepts a --context flag with a file path. When you use the "Send to Coder Agent" command, it will:

Save the current search results to a temporary Markdown file
Open a terminal
Execute the Coder agent with the context file and your query

This allows your Coder agent to have relevant project context when responding to your requests.